{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06GI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$x_0 \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{F}(k))$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$x_0$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$A$", "MATH_0007": "$x \\to q_*x$", "MATH_0008": "$q : A \\to k$", "MATH_0009": "$q_*x \\to x_0$", "MATH_0010": "$x \\to q_*x \\to x_0$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:88b2de164f47820ee9924d292d08fe6ccd6a0fd12fec9791b12f39fb2157f40e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9ccbfaabe23156b2584c623506e9b850ac79b3335b920efdbf1d571824794cd2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA feature of a predeformation category is the following.\nLet <MATH_0001>. Then every object of\n<MATH_0002> comes equipped with a unique morphism to <MATH_0003>.\nNamely, if <MATH_0004> is an object of <MATH_0005> over <MATH_0006>, then we\ncan choose a pushforward <MATH_0007> where <MATH_0008> is the quotient\nmap. There is a unique isomorphism <MATH_0009> and the composition\n<MATH_0010> is the desired morphism.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:42e95ec0fe3730660d905770ab14bfd163f669a9254bfb3dc68c7602017bfe79", "unit_id": "tag:06GI:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06GI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F: \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$F(k)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{F}}$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-predeformation-functor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:59d4f9f0d05524403091e8543af8999664aee620e14d0d102809e895d2f7da8e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:14ae4fe46528dfc554d592c2798c01fe7310af5b4c90a717ae869932325bd986", "source_text": "We say that a functor <MATH_0001>\nis a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>predeformation functor<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the associated cofibered set is a\npredeformation category, i.e.<SPACE_0001>if <MATH_0002> is a one element set.  Thus if\n<MATH_0003> is a predeformation category, then <MATH_0004> is a\npredeformation functor.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f68b8edae870f971a9cdb2e5fe6d8e9c4742207f574d55849074a885c88f5fe9", "unit_id": "tag:06GT:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06GI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{F}(k))$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0006": "$y \\to x$", "MATH_0007": "$(y \\to x) \\to (z \\to x)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\ny \\ar[rr] \\ar[dr] & & z \\ar[dl] \\\\\n& x &\n}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}_x \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0011": "$p_x : \\mathcal{F}_x \\to \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}_x \\to \\mathcal{F} \\xrightarrow{p} \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0013": "$p_x : \\mathcal{F}_x \\to \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0015": "$x \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{F}(k))$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-localize-cofibered-groupoid}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ac218fd3f84bfe250123af76893662a7e646ebd567dbf143d6b5190e27441a04", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1ff64d570c2543dbc263078e2376192bdf5b10aab60871bb75288cd7ec2e738e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category cofibered in\ngroupoids, and let <MATH_0002>.  We denote by\n<MATH_0003> the category of objects over <MATH_0004>.\nAn object of <MATH_0005> is an arrow <MATH_0006>.\nA morphism <MATH_0007> in <MATH_0008> is a commutative\ndiagram\n<MATH_0009>\nThere is a forgetful functor <MATH_0010>. We define\nthe functor <MATH_0011> as the\ncomposition\n<MATH_0012>.\nThen <MATH_0013> is a\npredeformation category (proof omitted). In this way we can pass from an\narbitrary category cofibered in groupoids over <MATH_0014>\nto a predeformation category at any <MATH_0015>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:efb5d17f5867012fa7a5f8d314df0dc7f2c88fd844d3c8fc8ff1ff77bcf945a4", "unit_id": "tag:06GU:statement"}
